01:13:10,909 --> 01:13:16,909
The Ring is a 2002 American supernatural horror film directed by Gore Verbinski, written by Ehren
Kruger, and starring Naomi Watts, Martin Henderson, David Dorfman, and Brian Cox.

15
01:18:24,545 --> 01:18:30,545
The film follows Rachel Keller, a journalist who discovers a cursed VHS
tape that causes its viewers to die seven days later.

16
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
It is the first installment in the American Ring series and a remake of the 1998
Japanese film, itself based on the 1991 novel by Koji Suzuki.

17
01:28:51,818 --> 01:28:57,818
The Ring was theatrically released in the United States by DreamWorks Pictures
on October 18, 2002, to mixed-to-positive reviews from critics.

18
01:34:05,454 --> 01:34:11,454
The film grossed $249.3 million worldwide and won Best Horror Film and
Best Actress (for Watts) at the 29th Saturn Awards.

19
01:39:19,090 --> 01:39:25,090
The success of The Ring inspired American remakes of several other Asian and
Japanese horror films, including The Grudge (2004) and Dark Water (2005).

20
01:44:32,727 --> 01:44:38,727
The film explores themes of journalist, island,
drowning, investigation, supernatural.

21
